{"term":"flute","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:4d09d1150637464360","definition":"A woodwind instrument consisting of a tube with a row of holes that produce sound through vibrations caused by air blown across the edge of the holes, often tuned by plugging one or more holes with a finger; the Western concert flute, a transverse side-blown flute of European origin.","example":"The breathing flute's ſoft notes are heard around, / And the ſhril trumpets mix their ſilver ſound; / The vaulted roofs vvith echoing muſic ring, / Theſe touch the vocal ſtops, and thoſe the trembling ſtring.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["Western concert flute","edge-blown aerophone"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["alto flute","block flute","chimney flute","devil's flute","Divje Babe flute","duct flute","en flute","English flute","eunuch flute","flute-bird","fluted armour","fluteful","fluteless","flutemouth","flute-player","fluter","flute register","flute stop","flutework","flutey","flutist","flutophone","fluty","German flute","hyperbass flute","Irish flute","Nason Flute","Native American flute","nose flute","octave flute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flute#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4bbc51a0206268606c","definition":"A recorder, also a woodwind instrument.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":["alto flute","block flute","chimney flute","devil's flute","Divje Babe flute","duct flute","en flute","English flute","eunuch flute","flute-bird","fluted armour","fluteful","fluteless","flutemouth","flute-player","fluter","flute register","flute stop","flutework","flutey","flutist","flutophone","fluty","German flute","hyperbass flute","Irish flute","Nason Flute","Native American flute","nose flute","octave flute"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.o